{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/222333-character-ideas-inspiration-motives-goals","id":222333,"title":"Character ideas, inspiration, motives, goals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-08T11:58:17-07:00","id":222333,"title":"Character ideas, inspiration, motives, goals","content":"Right now I'm experiencing an extreme lack in inspiration for characters, particularly for a Wraith character (my first Wraith, actually). I'm getting pretty desperate to be honest. I really detest this sort of malaise and need something to give me that spark.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that this is particularly due to me not reading much at all these days. When I would read, I had so many different ideas that it was insane.<br /> <br /> I guess my question now is that is there a place that gives prompts and/or inspiration for characters? Also, is there a place that gives specifically WoD styled character inspirations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T13:10:29-07:00","id":222404,"title":"","content":"I find Wraiths pretty challenging things to make. Do you have any ideas for what kind of regrets your character might have? This should help you come up with appropriate passions and fetters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T13:24:00-07:00","id":222418,"title":"","content":"Well that can be tricky. When I'm stumped like that I often read sample character concepts in the various splat books. In fact that's how I came up with my current V20 character. I was reading through the Clan Book sample character section, got an idea from them and used that as the backbone of the character. And they don't have to Wraith Guild Books either, just about any character concept from any splat book could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T14:21:24-07:00","id":222456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that this is particularly due to me not reading much at all these days. When I would read, I had so many different ideas that it was insane. </div> </div> </div>Well, I sparkle out with ideas when I read the Character Sheet or chapter with creating a character <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess my question now is that is there a place that gives prompts and/or inspiration for characters? Also, is there a place that gives specifically WoD styled character inspirations? </div> </div> </div>I don't exactly get what are you asking for?<br /> When I want graphic inspiration I run into deviantart and type words connecting to the mood of game in search for gloomy, sad photos, artworks. And the music runs in the background. Even dj shadow is good for Wraith, along with placebo etc. Songs about regrets and stuff..<br /> <br /> Maybe look for your own regrets. Or roll a dice to choose Life, Death of your character and suddenly you will end with firefighter who watched his collegues dying in flames or something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T14:41:22-07:00","id":222462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/222333-character-ideas-inspiration-motives-goals?p=222418#post222418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that can be tricky. When I'm stumped like that I often read sample character concepts in the various splat books. In fact that's how I came up with my current V20 character. I was reading through the Clan Book sample character section, got an idea from them and used that as the backbone of the character. And they don't have to Wraith Guild Books either, just about any character concept from any splat book could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing about Wraith is that it lacks the strong character archetypes that other games have. The Legions are only relevant if you are Hierarchy-aligned, and even then the way you died only means so much. The Guilds are disbanded, but if you had a favorite Arcanos you could always build toward that, but the core book has almost no information on the guilds, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T15:16:44-07:00","id":222506,"title":"","content":"Well the Guild Books do actually have sample character concepts and some of them are pretty good. And while the officially disbanded reality is a whole other story. In fact I've got a WtO would love to play as if I can ever get the group for it from the Artificers Guild Book sample characters.<br /> <br /> And besides that you could make a solid character from one of the other lines sample characters, with some tweaks here and there of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:56:06-07:00","id":222568,"title":"","content":"When I get stuck, I look at what the Storyteller plans for the game and what the other players are doing. I'll often be the last to put in a character, as I take a role that the group needs. (Of course, I'm normally a Storyteller, so helping Storytellers and other players is part of my approach.)<br /> <br /> For <b>Wraith: The Oblivion</b>, someone with Passions and Fetters that connect some of the other PCs and some major NPCs could be useful - <b>Wraith</b> characters can often get caught up in their personal drives rather than interacting with the group much. To use an example from an article in <b>White Wolf Inphobia</b> issue 50 about building character connections in <b>Wraith</b>, let's say one of the other characters was murdered by a street gang - if your character was robbed by them, or was a member of a rival gang, or has a building in their territory as a Fetter, this would give you a reason to work with her, at least for a while.<br /> <br /> Another way to look at it is to take advantage of <b>Wraith</b>'s unusual character creation and concentrate on the Shadow first. What does the character hate and fear, and what does the Psyche do about resisting the Shadow's desires to act on those violent feelings?<br /> <br /> The heavy psychological option to look at your life and imagine what you would be passionate about if you became a Wraith tomorrow can yield some interesting results, but might not be <i>fun</i> to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T21:13:07-07:00","id":222778,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This may sound a bit on the trite and silly side, but when I\u2019m stumped for characters (whether it\u2019s PCs or NPCs), I\u2019ll people-watch at a Starbucks. I grab a coffee, hang out for a few, and watch the Quick scamper on with their lives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:56:24-07:00","id":224336,"title":"","content":"One way to look at character inspiration is to consider it from the perspective of the gaming table. During a typical session, what do you want to <i><b>do</b></i>?<br /> <br /> Are you exciting about solving clues, talking your way out of situations, stirring up shit? Do you want a character who's got a strong person mission that they'll drag others along for, or someone who is innately inspired to collaborate and help other PCs? What kind of personality might it be fun to roleplay? Are you going to be boldly impulsive, or careful and reserved but come up with convoluted plans?<br /> <br /> The answers to these questions don't amount to a fleshed out character on their own, but they can give you a spark or scaffold to start from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:03:08-07:00","id":224389,"title":"","content":"Honestly, to me it comes easly.<br /> <br /> when i run games of Demon the Fallen i have the following rule. You can create the Demon (i mean work the lores , name, house ) but I give you a human. i offer you 3 humans who you can possess and i writte them up. this gives me the chance to think and ponder of humans who lost everything.<br /> <br /> also, reading a lot.<br /> <br /> let me give you a weapon, a tool or technique that i use to writte Wraith characters.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XF3xCifQ290\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XF3xCifQ290\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XF3xCifQ290\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XF3xCifQ290 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I hear a lot of silent hill soundtrack whenever i run a game of wraith or i think about a character. I start coming up with the looks of the character. When i first created David Torien (My Wraith char) first i took elements i thought they would work on a story. these were Tragedy and Love.<br /> <br /> Then, having that basis i thought on his apparience. Id magine him as a very thin guy, mid 20's, always covering one eye with a lock of hair and wearing long sleeve glovesand rags around his wrists, looking very sad but with a permanent smile.<br /> <br /> i have this mental iamge and i give it a name &quot;The Comedian.&quot; then i see the scars his body has and i start working out How he died, David was one time stand up comedian, he was tortured (hence the glasglow smile), his hands were burned and finally, he was shoot on the eye.<br /> <br /> Now i know how he died, then i work out. But who was him before his death?, i want to take the elements of love and tragedy.<br /> Whats the tragedy element?, he is inlove with a woman named Anne, he was going to propose her but he never could (first passion). After he died, she stop being a woman who makes the world shine and became dark and gloomy, got into ouija and slowly become self destructive, David wishes to save her, to avoid her life to be miserable and for her to rise again, to enjoy the time of her life so she never ends up on The Underworld (Second passion, Protection).<br /> The place he loved the most was the couch, where he played videogames, watched movies, and spend most time with Anne, its their special nest. even if he find it on the trash (First Fetter), He was a slacker, theres no doubt about that. the secodn thing he appreciated was his NES, was a gift from his older brother who passed away on Irak. he could replace the old NES with any next gen console, but that was the first &quot;Toy&quot; he learned how to use, and how his brother took the time to teach his stupid little brother how to beat Legend of Zelda. (Second Fetter). The third fetter is the Engagement ring.<br /> <br /> What does the shadow Wants? the shadow is everyones darkness. David sort of accepted his death, but he doesnt know why he was killed, was a bad joke? was because he looked fragile?- The shadow wants him to commit murder, to go back to the land of the quick and kill them bastards, to torture them, to show them that the comedian is laughing again. to make David loose whats left of his humanity just for the sake of payback. David is afraid of loosing his humanity on this land known as Stygia, he feels that if he looses that, he will become a monster who wont be able to recognize the ones he loves and cares about. his battle is to keep his empathy.<br /> <br /> And thats how i created one character (feel free to use him on your games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}